          "name": "Chrome Extension Client Key",
          "request": {
            "name": "Chrome Extension Client Key",
            "description": {
              "content": "Pre-auth bootstrap endpoint for the Chrome extension.\n\nThe extension does NOT have an org API key. It exchanges an install ID for a short-lived `client_key`\n(JWT) which can be used to connect to `/client_ws` or `/client_ws_v2`.\n\n**Preferred (header-based):** pass the token via the ``Sec-WebSocket-Protocol`` header::\n\n    new WebSocket(url, [\"access_token\", clientKey])\n\n**Legacy (query-param):** ``/client_ws?client_key=<JWT>`` is still supported for\nbackward compatibility but is discouraged because tokens in URLs can appear in\nserver access logs.",
              "type": "text/plain"
            },
            "url": {
              "path": [
